From a473175dd8183b53be43769b7383ce67faa8dff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:08:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Fix dark mode contrast, disable duplicate cash in split
 payment, add Payment Complete modal, and add Transaction Record + End of Day
 Reconciliation

Dark mode fix
- Root cause: several buttons/pills/badges (active sidebar link, primary
  buttons, avatar, Complete Sale button, toasts, scanner tabs) used
  var(--pos-ink) as a dark BACKGROUND fill with white text on top.
  Dark mode redefined --pos-ink to a near-white TEXT color, which
  turned every one of those into invisible white-on-white.
- Fix: added a constant --pos-fill-dark (unaffected by theme) for
  those specific dark chip/button backgrounds, and repointed all of
  them to it. --pos-ink stays theme-aware for text everywhere else.
- Added dark-mode polish for dropdown items, .btn-close, list groups,
  and icon-button hover states.

Checkout modal: split payment
- A split payment could previously have 'Cash' selected in more than
  one row (double-counting toward change-due math). The Cash option is
  now disabled (with an 'already used' label) in every row once
  another row has already selected it.

Payment Complete modal
- New confirmation modal shown immediately after Complete Sale, before
  the printable receipt: invoice number, amount paid, change due, a
  20-second auto-advancing progress bar, and a Done button to skip the
  wait and go straight to the receipt.
- POSController::checkout() now also returns invoice_no (via new
  Sale::getInvoiceNumber()) so the confirmation can show it without an
  extra request.

Transaction Record & End of Day Reconciliation (new page)
- New app/models/Reconciliation.php, app/controllers/ReconciliationController.php,
  views/reconciliation.php, reconciliation.php entry point, and
  assets/js/reconciliation.js, linked from the sidebar.
- Transaction Record: every transaction for a chosen business date
  (register-tape style), with a running completed-sales total.
- End of Day Reconciliation: expected cash is computed from actual
  SalePayments rows (cash portion only - a split cash+card sale only
  counts its cash share) plus opening float, minus change paid out;
  compared against a manually counted amount to produce an over/short
  variance. Saved per business_date (upsert) in the new
  CashReconciliation table, with the next day's opening float
  auto-suggested from the prior day's counted cash.
- New database/migration_cash_reconciliation.sql for existing installs;
  pos_store.sql updated for fresh ones.
