From 9aec392d6d854b7f0dcafc9ca62cbbf1c5522482 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:06:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Move End of Day into Reconciliation page; replace inline
 price/discount fields with Edit Price / Add Discount modals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

End of Day
- Removed the 'End of Day' button, modal, and reconciliation.js include
  from the POS Screen entirely.
- Reconciliation page now leads with Transaction Record as the main
  (full-width) content, plus a new 'End of Day' button next to the
  date navigation. Clicking it opens a modal with the cash-drawer
  details: payment breakdown, opening float, cash collected, change
  given out, expected cash, counted cash, variance, notes, and Save.

POS cart: price/discount now open modals instead of inline textboxes
- Each cart row now shows a compact price chip (e.g. '₱12.00/pc' with
  a pencil icon) and a discount chip (tag icon), instead of always-on
  number inputs.
- Clicking the price chip opens 'Edit Price': item name, old price,
  and a new-price box capped at the catalog price, with 'Update
  Price'.
- Clicking the discount chip opens 'Add discount on this item': item
  name, original price, a discount value with a ₱/% toggle, a
  live-updating new price, and 'Apply discount'.
- Fixed two dead/invalid CSS rules for the discount chip's 'active'
  state (empty rule bodies, one referencing the jQuery-only
  :contains() pseudo-class, which isn't valid CSS) - replaced with a
  real .pos-cart-chip-active style and wired the class onto the chip
  when a discount is applied.
